# 8x10 seated character seen from BEHIND — the desk pose for a back-turned seat
# (`HomeDesk::facing`), and the fallback for every seated pose whose own back
# view the pack does not ship.
#
# The HEAD keeps the front view's six rows. That proportion is not a bug to fix:
# `seated.sprite` spends the same six on hair + face, so both silhouettes are one
# head over one torso. An earlier revision of this file claimed the six rows made
# it "read as a ball" and added a NECK to break them up — wrong twice over. The
# front view has no neck at all (its chin row meets the shoulders directly), so
# it invented an organ the pack's own language does not use, and at 2 px wide it
# was the sub-pixel detail this art scale cannot render anyway.
#
# What actually differs from the front is INTERNAL STRUCTURE: a face carries
# eyes, a mouth and a hairline, while the back of a head is one flat colour. If
# that ever needs breaking up, the lever is SHADING (an `n` band low on the
# skull) — shape, which reads at half-block — not another feature.
#
# The hands ARE kept: `.SBBBBS.` is row 9 of `seated.sprite` verbatim, so the two
# views read as the same person, and they carry the only skin a back view can
# honestly show. That matters because per-agent identity is hair + skin
# (`agent_id`-seeded) while the outfit is cwd-seeded and SHARED across a repo's
# agents — but two pixels is all this angle affords, and losing the rest is a
# property of facing away, not a defect to engineer around.
@frame 0
. n H H H H n .
n H H H H H H n
H H H H H H H H
H H H H H H H H
. H H H H H H .
. n H H H H n .
. B B B B B B .
B B B B B B B B
B B B B B B B B
. S B B B B S .
